@@@ note
A `[!NOTE]` marker alone on a blockquote's first line is GitHub's alert syntax. It has to
keep its own line and stay unescaped even when the width would otherwise let it share a
line with the body — merging it in turns a styled callout back into a plain quote holding
literal `\[!NOTE\]` text. See #17.

@@@ input
> [!NOTE]
> Some information worth calling out, long enough that it wraps across more than
> one line on its own.

@@@ wrap 80
> [!NOTE]
> Some information worth calling out, long enough that it wraps across more than
> one line on its own.

@@@ wrap 200
> [!NOTE]
> Some information worth calling out, long enough that it wraps across more than one line on its own.

@@@ unwrap
> [!NOTE]
> Some information worth calling out, long enough that it wraps across more than one line on its own.
